    <title>Chief Complaint</title>
    <text><paragraph>Six-week review: healing after the extraction, diabetes, eye and foot screening, and cardiovascular risk. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Hatshepsut returns six weeks after the extraction. The socket healed without trouble and she finished the two weeks of chlorhexidine; she is chewing on both sides again. She takes metformin 1000 mg with the evening meal without stomach upset. Her thirst and night urination have eased. She has been to two of the diabetes education and nutrition sessions and has cut down on sweet tea and dates. She would like to lose some weight to make the stairs easier, and asks about the weekly injections she has read about. Her knees hurt less since she began the strengthening exercises and the gel. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Mouth</td><td>Socket healed; chewing on both sides</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes</td><td>Metformin 1000 mg tolerated; two education sessions; thirst eased</td></tr><tr><td>Her goal</td><td>Climb stairs at the sites more easily; interested in a GLP-1 medicine</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
